  "id": "session-switch-walk",
  "title": "Historical session switching, walking the session list",
  "description": "Two processes each walk the session list consecutively, top to bottom, twice: the first pass opens every session for the first time and the second pass returns to each in the same order. The list is the corpus's own recency order, workspace-b newest first and then workspace-a newest first, which the workspace-contiguous corpus makes identical in lists grouped by workspace and lists sorted by recency; the control session the app launches on is not walked. One separate process runs the 1/8 MiB progressive memory workload sampled by the framework.",
